[00:39.27]As the spring breeze blew, life began anew
[00:44.84]Like the endless passion of recurring wildfires
[00:51.39]The good old days
[00:55.67]By the wind and rain are swept away
[01:05.43]From tears you come
[01:10.44]And in laughter you shall go
[01:17.51]The coming days are precious
[01:20.41]Tomorrow will worry about itself
[01:31.53]In a maze, interminable
[01:36.51]In a chess game, inevitable
[01:42.81]Atop the tall hill
[01:46.11]The willows refresh annually, so green anew
[02:56.77]Upon the lush mountain, in endless sight
[03:01.97]Printed my tracks, go after you
[03:07.87]Aroused by the soft dance
[03:11.18]As the rain patters on men and leaves
[03:21.92]The incessant urge
[03:27.41]Echoes through my mind when close to you
[03:33.60]At the crossroads
[03:36.75]A sorrow as spring on high